  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "Heat 1 tbsp oil in a wok on medium-high. Add mushrooms, ginger, and 1 tbsp water. Stir-fry until browned and softened, about 2 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Add another 1 tbsp oil, water chestnuts, and 1 tbsp water. Fry for another minute."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Add the remaining oil, sugar snap peas, and water. Fry for another 2 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Season with soy sauce and salt to taste."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Serve."
    }
  ],
  "attribution": {
    "name": "Jean-Georges Vongerichten"
  },
  "notes": "Crunchy, salty, and sweet, this quick stir-fry takes advantage of fresh vegetables by treating them simply. A hint of ginger and a splash of soy sauce are all you need. Blanched sugar snap peas: boil for 1 minute, then plunge in ice water immediately.",
